# X. Intellect: unity that knows its own differentiation

From proposition 160 onward, Proclus develops intellect.

Intellect is not merely a processor.

It is a structure in which:

* knower;
* knowing;
* known

remain distinct but internally unified.

Intellect returns upon itself:

[
N
\rightarrow
N.
]

Its object is not externally alien to it. The intelligible content is internally present within the act of intellection.

But intellect is not the One.

It is already articulated:

[
N
=

{n_1,n_2,\ldots}
]

held within noetic unity.

This is Proclus’s equivalent of a reflexively structured field.

## Relation to vimarśa

The closest Śaiva parallel is:

[
\textit{vimarśa}.
]

Both reject inert luminosity.

Manifestness becomes determinate only through a power by which it articulates:

[
\text{this}
]

as distinct from:

[
\text{that}.
]

But Proclus places reflexive articulation at the level of intellect and soul, beneath the One.

Abhinavagupta places reflexivity in the absolute itself.

That difference is decisive:

[
\boxed{
\text{Proclus: the ultimate exceeds reflexive subjectivity;}
}
]

[
\boxed{
\text{Abhinavagupta: the ultimate is reflexive subjectivity.}
}
]

