# XII. What “return” means for recognition

The *Elements* does not provide a full theory of contemplative recognition. It is principally an ontological treatise.

But its metaphysics implies a recognitional structure.

A participant initially encounters itself as:

[
P_i
===

\text{apparently independent finite being}.
]

Proclean understanding reveals:

[
P_i
===

\operatorname{Participant}
\left(
u_i,U
\right).
]

Recognition changes:

[
\text{distinction-as-independence}
]

into:

[
\text{distinction-as-participation}.
]

Formally:

[
\mathcal R_i^{\mathrm{Proclus}}:
\operatorname{SelfModel}
\left(
P_i=\operatorname{SelfGrounding}
\right)
]

[
\longrightarrow
]

[
\operatorname{SelfModel}
\left(
P_i
===

\operatorname{DistinctParticipation}(U)
\right).
]

This is a reversion because the participant becomes reflectively oriented toward the source already causally present within it.

## What remains unchanged

Recognition does not destroy:

* participant identity;
* local perspective;
* causal role;
* finite power;
* hierarchy;
* distinct field.

Thus:

[
\boxed{
\text{recognition removes imagined independence,}
}
]

not:

[
\boxed{
\text{real distinction}.
}
]

This is a profound correction to poorly formulated nondualism.

