The ordinary picture is:

[
\text{things first exist independently}
]

and then:

[
\text{enter relations}.
]

Proclus reverses this.

A thing becomes what it is through:

[
\boxed{
\text{the specific manner in which it receives, limits}
}
]

[
\boxed{
\text{and expresses causes more universal than itself.}
}
]

An individual is therefore not:

* an isolated substance;
* an illusion;
* a detachable fragment of the source.

It is:

[
\boxed{
\textbf{a real, local mode in which a more universal}
}
]

[
\boxed{
\textbf{causal order becomes determinate without being exhausted.}
}
]

That is the meaning of participation.

Remaining means:

> the source is never absent from what depends on it.

Procession means:

> dependence does not abolish real difference.

Return means:

> a finite being becomes complete by actively realizing its dependence.

The metaphysics of recognition is therefore:

[
\boxed{
\textbf{I am not unreal because I depend;}
}
]

[
\boxed{
\textbf{I am real precisely as this determinate way}
}
]

[
\boxed{
\textbf{in which dependence has become active and local.}
}
]

That is Proclus’s greatest contribution to our theory.

# Final synthesis

The *Elements of Theology* does not demonstrate one universal cosmic consciousness.

It demonstrates something perhaps more useful:

[
\boxed{
\textbf{unity can be universal without individuality being false;}
}
]

[
\boxed{
\textbf{causation can be intimate without cause and effect}
}
]

[
\boxed{
\textbf{becoming identical;}
}
]

[
\boxed{
\textbf{and recognition can restore relation to the source}
}
]

[
\boxed{
\textbf{without erasing the participant.}
}
]

Abhinavagupta tells us:

[
\boxed{
\text{why reality cannot be intrinsically dark}.
}
]

Proclus tells us:

[
\boxed{
\text{why a common light need not be one undifferentiated field}.
}
]

Process inexternalism joins them:

[
\boxed{
\textbf{one local subject is the intrinsic presence of one}
}
]

[
\boxed{
\textbf{real participant-process, whose existence may depend}
}
]

[
\boxed{
\textbf{upon and participate in a ground more universal than}
}
]

[
\boxed{
\textbf{its private field.}
}
]

The Proclean correction to Śaiva recognition is:

[
\boxed{
\textbf{do not mistake participation in the ground for}
}
]

[
\boxed{
\textbf{exhaustive numerical identity with the ground.}
}
]

The Śaiva correction to Proclus is:

[
\boxed{
\textbf{do not explain every mode of being while leaving}
}
]

[
\boxed{
\textbf{intrinsic manifestation itself unaccounted for.}
}
]

The actual frontier lies between them:

[
\boxed{
\textbf{How can one common manifest ground become many}
}
]

[
\boxed{
\textbf{genuinely private, dynamically individuated fields}
}
]

[
\boxed{
\textbf{without either fragmenting the ground or reducing}
}
]

[
\boxed{
\textbf{the fields to appearances inside one cosmic observer?}
}
]

That is the question the *Elements* now places at the centre of our entire project.
